ng Sine and Cosine" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050718 #edb/ref 1033 1491 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050718 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "61092d2e-5ae6-5f60-8a88-2299822508ec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050753 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048118 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050753 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049528 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050753 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049745 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050753 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050753 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186129152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050753 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186129153 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050753 #edb/ref 1031 "Graphing the Square Root Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050753 #edb/ref 1033 2038 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050753 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "63beb30b-812d-5842-a68b-ba473953a810" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114915 #edb/ref 1069 "e-1122" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114915 #edb/ref 1071 "In which intervals is the function $y=f(x)$ (plotted below) strictly increasing? In which intervals is it increasing?\n\n![](images/cf/cfe907d96b0b9ee70fa48922b398baee66fe4bfded024134604bfb3a15c7c013.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114915 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "514bbf6e-7eb5-5158-ac3f-5cb1f88d72d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114915 #edb/ref 1074 "If we follow the graph from left to right, we can see that: \n\n- For $x\\in(-2,2)$ the graph rises\n\n- For $x\\in(2,5)$ the graph falls\n\n- For $x\\in(5,7)$ the graph is flat\n\n- For $x\\in(7,9)$ the graph rises\n\nTherefore, we conclude that:\n\n- The function is *strictly increasing* on the intervals where it always rises: $(-2,2)$ and $(7,9).$\n\n- The function is *increasing* on the intervals where it never falls: $(-2,2)$ and $(5,9).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114916 #edb/ref 1069 "e-1123" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114916 #edb/ref 1071 "In which intervals is the function $y=f(x)$ 