5b2e-9ad5-d70273d4a38d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116271 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186116430 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116272 #edb/ref 1061 3661 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116272 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7450e4ef-df70-5ca4-8c6d-12844e5fe1ad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116272 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186115338 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116429 #edb/ref 1064 "A function ![](images/93/93f888a1ee0b7da5e29f442f803f1c0eaf73ad02f5eaa97e85bb8a35d607015b.svg) is **strictly increasing** if its ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-value always rises as we increase the ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg)-value. No section of the graph is allowed to be flat.\n\n![](images/f6/f6136545f441473a1c873f7d3296e8d96c23357825ac442ce83ce313f2d74199.png)\n\nOn the other hand, a function ![](images/93/93f888a1ee0b7da5e29f442f803f1c0eaf73ad02f5eaa97e85bb8a35d607015b.svg) is **increasing** if its ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-value *never falls* as we increase the ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg)-value. \n\n**Watch Out!** Increasing functions, like the one below, are allowed to have flat sections.\n\n![](images/b9/b979741f27906322c7ff290ae37bb5214c0c88d30e504fe18569c1f957e3d72e.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116429 #edb/ref 1065 1500 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116429 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "75e3de1d-9fd6-536a-b21e-7d6434297ce7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116429 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116430 #edb/ref 1064 "A function $f(x)$ is **strictly decreasing** if its $y$-value always *falls* as we increase the $x$-value. No section of the graph is allowed to be flat.\n\n![](images/b8/b8a2d54cedc84f159a61bfccc11bdab9adc73eb54b694dd1167802998f4d39d3.png)\n\nOn the other hand, a function $f(x)$ is **decreasing** i